questions.stem:
While auditing locker numbers, a program binary-searches this sorted list:
int[] data = {4, 11, 18, 25, 33, 40};
int lo = 0, hi = 5;
It computes mid as (lo + hi) / 2 and compares data[mid] with target 25. Which index is examined first?

A warehouse routine narrows its window with this fragment:
while (lo <= hi) {
  int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
  if (data[mid] == target) return mid;
  if (data[mid] > target) { _____; }
  else { lo = mid + 1; }
}
Which line belongs in the blank?

After fueling, a pit crew orders four tire pressures with one selection-sort pass that swaps the minimum into index 0:
int[] p = {44, 12, 38, 5};
What order results from that single pass?

While ranking chili peppers, a judge runs two full selection-sort passes over this row:
int[] heat = {50, 9, 41, 23};
Each pass swaps the minimum of the unsorted region into place. What order results after both passes?

While shelving returned novels, a clerk runs the first insertion-sort step (i = 1) on this shelf:
int[] shelf = {30, 12, 25};
The step inserts 12 into the sorted prefix. What order results?

A mailroom inserts parcels by arrival time with this fragment:
for (int i = 1; i < a.length; i++) {
  int key = a[i];
  int j = i;
  while (j > 0 && a[j - 1] > key) { _____; j--; }
  a[j] = key;
}
Which line belongs in the blank?

Before dawn a bakery's insertion sort crashes with this inner loop:
while (j >= 0 && a[j - 1] > key) { a[j] = a[j - 1]; j--; }
What is the fault?

A referee trims even badge numbers while scanning forward:
ArrayList<Integer> ids = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(6, 2, 9, 4));
for (int i = 0; i < ids.size(); i++) { if (ids.get(i) % 2 == 0) ids.remove(i); }
What remains in the list?

A club roster edit crashes at run time here:
for (String s : roster) { if (s.startsWith("X")) roster.remove(s); }
What is the fault?

A dispatcher purges even dockets by scanning backward so shifts never hide entries:
for (int i = _____; i >= 0; i--) { if (nums.get(i) % 2 == 0) nums.remove(i); }
Which start belongs in the blank?

A print spooler drains every rush job with this loop:
ArrayList<Integer> line = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(5, 5, 5));
int i = 0;
while (i < line.size()) { if (line.get(i) == 5) line.remove(i); else i++; }
What does the list hold afterward?

A scorekeeper compares two boxed totals with this fragment:
Integer a = 200;
Integer b = 200;
System.out.println(a == b);
What is printed?

A payroll helper adds an unset bonus with this fragment:
Integer bonus = null;
int total = bonus + 10;
What happens when it runs?

A coach totals boxed points with this loop:
int total = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < pts.size(); i++) { total += _____; }
Here pts is an ArrayList<Integer>. Which expression belongs in the blank?

A fitness challenge sums only strong laps with this fragment:
ArrayList<Integer> pts = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(6, 3, 9));
int t = 0;
for (int v : pts) { if (v > 4) t += v; }
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?
